&& flag != \"--equal\") { ... existing, maybe include --empty in known ... }\n    ...\n}\n```\n\nNote there's a subtlety: currently the \"unknown flag\" check happens after the argc check. If someone passes `--empty a b`, argc=4 passes first check then flag is empty → unknown → ok. But we handle `--empty` before. Good. If `--empty` alone (argc=2) → our branch handles, prints \"1 argument expected\". Good.\n\nShould `--empty` be added to the list in the unknown-flag message? Yes, \"Expected --contains, --equal or --empty\". But since `--empty` is handled early, the unknown branch won't see it. Still update message for accuracy.\n\nThe `--empty` output should be on raw bytes without normalization. `file_to_bytes_string` returns raw. Good.\n\nAlso consider: should we print using `escape_window`? It's in anonymous namespace defined above main — accessible. Good.\n\n### tests/CMakeLists.txt changes\nAfter computing `PROGRAMM_RESULT` and `RESULT_TEST` (lines 109-115), add the \"other\" channel:\n\n```cmake\n# тихий канал - тот, что не выбран stream. он обязан быть пуст\nif(${stream} EQUAL 1)\n  set(SILENT_FILE ${STDERR_FILE})\n  set(EMPTY_TEST \"${test_name}_stderr_empty\")\nelseif(${stream} EQUAL 2)\n  set(SILENT_FILE ${STDOUT_FILE})\n  set(EMPTY_TEST \"${test_name}_stdout_empty\")\nendif()\n\nadd_test(NAME ${EMPTY_TEST} COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:check> --empty ${SILENT_FILE})\nset_tests_properties(${EMPTY_TEST} PROPERTIES FIXTURES_REQUIRED ${test_name})\n```\n\nBetter to combine with the existing if/elseif to avoid duplication:\n```cmake\nif(${stream} EQUAL 1)\n  set(PROGRAMM_RESULT ${STDOUT_FILE})\n  set(RESULT_TEST \"${test_name}_stdout\")\n  set(SILENT_FILE ${STDERR_FILE})\n  set(EMPTY_TEST \"${test_name}_stderr_empty\")\nelseif(${stream} EQUAL 2)\n  set(PROGRAMM_RESULT ${STDERR_FILE})\n  set(RESULT_TEST \"${test_name}_stderr\")\n  set(SILENT_FILE ${STDOUT_FILE})\n  set(EMPTY_TEST \"${test_name}_stdout_empty\")\nendif()\n```\n\nPlace `add_test`/`set_tests_properties` after the existing RESULT_TEST block, near lines 125-142.\n\nNote: `check` needs to be built before tests run — CMake add_test with `$<TARGET_FILE:check>` creates the dependency automatically? For CTest, `$<TARGET_FILE:check>` in add_test COMMAND does register a dependency (CMake docs: using generator expression target file creates a target-level dependency). Actually `run_case`/`check` already used this way. Good.\n\n### Verification\nCommands:\n- `cmake --preset debug`\n- `cmake --build build/debug`\n- `ctest --preset full` → expect 100% and count ~1043.\n- Negative control: e.g., in a success task write `std::println(stderr, \"probe\")` temporarily; rebuild; `ctest --test-dir build/debug -R \"_stderr_empty\" --output-on-failure` → expect failures. Revert. Similarly for a stdout write on an error path → `_stdout_empty`.\n- Release: `cmake --preset release`, build, `ctest --preset full-release`.\n- VM: same.\n\nWait — a concern: negative control for the \"silent\" test. But if we modify a success task to write to stderr, the existing `_stdout` test still passes and only `_stderr_empty` fails. Good, precise.\n\nAnother concern: Does modifying product tasks risk leaving artifacts? We revert; must ensure `git diff` clean afterwards.\n\nThere's an even cleaner negative control that doesn't touch product code: temporarily edit one expect file? No, that tests the compared channel, not empty. The wrong-channel write is the honest probe.\n\nAlso, I should think about whether `check --empty` should be used for both error/success. Yes.\n\n### Count / runtime\n781 → ~1043. mention.\n\n### README\nLine 73 update: add `--empty` mode.\n\n### Journal/CHANGELOG\nThe user maintains; mention as follow-up not part of code.\n\nNow, the plan is complete. Since plan mode forbids edits, I present the final plan and ask to proceed (or the user will switch modes). Per the harness, the user must approve / exit plan mode. I'll present the plan concisely and say ready to implement once out of pl