rt with a different code and stderr containing ASan report; the new empty-stdout test would likely still pass (stdout empty). Good.\n\nSo, answer concisely: For your project — yes, the rule is right and worth enforcing, because your programs have exactly two modes with no overlap and no progress stream. It's not \"some programs do both, so my rule is wrong\" — it's a contract of *your* task class. Document it as an invariant. If/when a task gains independent diagnostic output alongside results (layer 11 logging or a --verbose that prints progress to stderr while results go to stdout), then you'll need both channels compared and the rule relaxed — decide *then*, don't build now.\n\nI should also give the distinction: what breaks and what it costs to add later. Two-channel support means add_case would need to compare both channels, i.e., a second result test; that's a localized extension, cheap when needed. The empty-check hardcode doesn't paint into a corner.\n\nCategorize with [ФАКТ/МНЕНИЕ/ПРЕДПОЛОЖЕНИЕ] and confidence.\n\nKeep it brief as she asked (\"кратко ответь\"). But she also wants reasoning. I'll be concise.\n\nLet me write ~10-15 lines.\n\nAlso mention: `2>b.txt` doesn't prove both non-empty; it just captures both. But yes programs exist that do both (e.g., ffmpeg: data vs progress). [ФАКТ].\n\nAnswer structure:\n- короткий вывод\n- почему для проекта ок\n- когда станет неверно и что тогда делать\n- caveat (partial stdout before failure)\n\nLet me draft.",
