          "text": "The user asks: create the 4 expect files by copying bytes from the C HELP_TEXT. Only 4 files, nothing else, don't build or run.\n\nI need to:\n- For each of t1..t4, read the C main.c, extract the HELP_TEXT literal bytes, decode `\\n`→LF and `\\\"`→`\"`, write to tests/expect/t{1..4}_help.\n\nByte-level, CP1251-safe. Round-trip lossless for CP1251 (verified for cli.c; the mains also CP1251). But to be safe, I'll do byte-level extraction WITHOUT decoding the whole file as text? I'll read bytes, scan for the HELP_TEXT assignment, extract quoted segments, decode escapes at byte level, write bytes. This avoids any encoding round-trip of the Russian.\n\nLet me write a PowerShell script that:\n1. Reads the file bytes.\n2. Finds the byte index of the ASCII substring `HELP_TEXT[] =`.\n3. From there, scans bytes; when it sees `\"` (0x22), starts a segment; reads until unescaped `\"`; within, handle escapes: `\\n`→0x0A, `\\\"`→0x22; other `\\x`? only these two expected. Collect into output list.\n4. Stops at `;` (0x3B) after the last `\"`.\n5. Writes the collected bytes to tests/expect/tN_help.\n\nActually, I must be careful about the scanning: after `HELP_TEXT[] =`, there are multiple `\"...\"` literals separated by whitespace/newlines, terminated by `;`. So:\n- i = index after `HELP_TEXT[] =`.\n- loop: skip whitespace; if current byte is `;` → done. if current byte is `\"` → parse literal; else error.\n- parse literal: j=i+1; while bytes[j] != 0x22 (unescaped): if bytes[j]==0x5C (backslash): next = bytes[j+1]; if next==0x6E ('n') append 0x0A; elif next==0x22 ('\"') append 0x22; elif next==0x5C append 0x5C; else append next (fallback); j+=2. else append bytes[j]; j+=1. Then i=j+1 (skip closing quote).\n\nLet me implement.\n\nThe expected output bytes = the decoded text (with internal LFs), no trailing newline. The program prints `text + \\n`; check strips trailing → fine.\n\nLet me write the script. Use .NET List[byte].\n\nLet me be careful: `HELP_TEXT[] =` — the exact text. Let me verify each C files uses `static const char HELP_TEXT[] =`. Yes (t1: `static const char HELP_TEXT[] =`). Good.\n\nLet me write the command.\n\nI'll produce a reusable function.\n\nPowerShell:\n\n```powershell\n$base='C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\inobitec_stud'\n$map=@{ 't1_help'='t1_dist_matrix_c\\main.c'; 't2_help'='t2_passport_c\\main.c'; 't3_help'='t3_bbox_c\\main.c'; 't4_help'='t4_filter_c\\main.c' }\nfunction Extract-Help([byte[]]$b){\n  $needle=[Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetBytes('HELP_TEXT[] =')\n  # find\n  $idx=-1\n  for($i=0;$i -le $b.Length-$needle.Length;$i++){ $ok=$true; for($k=0;$k -lt $needle.Length;$k++){ if($b[$i+$k] -ne $needle[$k]){ $ok=$false; break } }; if($ok){ $idx=$i; break } }\n  if($idx -lt 0){ throw 'HELP_TEXT not found' }\n  $out=New-Object System.Collections.Generic.List[byte]\n  $i=$idx+$needle.Length\n  while($i -lt $b.Length){\n    $c=$b[$i]\n    if($c -eq 0x3B){ break } # ;\n    if($c -eq 0x22){ # opening quote\n      $i++\n      while($i -lt $b.Length -and $b[$i] -ne 0x22){\n        if($b[$i] -eq 0x5C){ # backslash\n          $n=$b[$i+1]\n          if($n -eq 0x6E){ $out.Add([byte]10) }        # \\n\n          elseif($n -eq 0x22){ $out.Add([byte]0x22) }  # \\\"\n          elseif($n -eq 0x5C){ $out.Add([byte]0x5C) }  # \\\\\n          else { $out.Add([byte]$n) }\n          $i+=2\n        } else {\n          $out.Add([byte]$b[$i]); $i++\n        }\n      }\n      $i++ # skip closing quote\n    } else {\n      $i++ # skip whitespace/newline between literals\n    }\n  }\n  return $out.ToArray()\n}\nforeach($k in $map.Keys){\n  $path=Join-Path $base ('tests\\expect\\'+$k)  # no, source is main.c\n}\n```\n\nWait, I mixed. Let me structure: for each expect name -> source file; extract; write to tests/expect/<expect name>.\n\n```powershell\nforeach($name in $map.Keys){\n  $src=Join-Path $base $map[$name]\n  $b=[IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($src)\n  $bytes=Extract-Help $b\n  [IO.File]::WriteAllBytes((Join-Path $base 'tests\\expect\\'+$name), $bytes)\n  \"$name <- $($map[$name]) : $($bytes.Length) bytes\"\n}\n```\n\nCareful: `$map.Keys` order arbitrary; fine.\n\nBut wait — writing `tests\\expect\\t1_help` etc. — the user said \"только 4 файла, ничего более\". Good.\n\nAlso, ensure the function handles the case where after `HELP_TEXT[] =` there's `\\r\\n    \"...\"`. The whitespace skip handles it.\n\nEdge: the `static const char HELP_TEXT[] =` — the needle `HELP_TEXT[] =` includes a space before `=`. Let me check exact: `static const char HELP_TEXT[] =` → yes `HELP_TEXT[] =`. Good. (t1 C: `static const char HELP_TEXT[] =`.)\n\nLet me also make sure the search doesn't match `kHelpText` (that's C++, not in C files). Fine.\n\nLet me run it.\n\nThen verify by decoding one expect and comparing length to expected. Also compare C++ raw text? Not needed.\n\nActually the user said \"не прогоняй\" (don't run). Running a PowerShell extraction script is not \"running the project/tests\". It's creating the files. That's allowed. They meant don't build/run the test suite. Good.\n\nLet me also NOT build/run anything else.\n\nLet me execute.\n\nOne more: verify the generated bytes decode correctly to Russian (spot check) — reading/decoding is fine (not running project). Let me do a quick decode of one file to include in output.\n\nLet me write and run.\n\nLet me double-check the escape handling for `\\\"`: In t3 C, the literal line: `\"Вход (stdin): точки \\\"x y z\\\" (по одной в строке) до EOF.\\n\"`. Bytes: ... 5C 22 ... The scan: at 0x5C, next is 0x22 → add 0x22, skip 2. Good → outputs `\"`. And `\\n` → LF. Good.\n\nLet me run.\n\nAlso handle the final: after the last literal's closing quote, next byte is `;` → break. Good.\n\nLet me code it carefully and run.",
