          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "The user asks about the 284/291 contradiction resolution: the mentor said to look at how known utilities do it and imitate them. The user did probes of git, cmake, cl on --help/-h/--helpp/--help extra. They ask:\n- Do I advise testing other utilities?\n- They see clearly: clean help → stdout; error → stderr + hint. But they have a doubt: maybe on error \"in the help flag itself\" → stderr, but \"--help smth_strange\" → stdout? Because only git throws to stderr in that case (it seems git expects something after help).\n\nI need to analyze and give my opinion, plan-mode (read-only, no edits).\n\nLet me think carefully about the observed behaviors:\n\n1. `git --help` / `-h` → stdout, exit 0. ✓\n2. `git --helpp` → error + hint, all stderr, exit != 0. (unknown flag)\n3. `git --help me` → git treats \"me\" as a subcommand? \"git --help me\" → git tries to show help for command \"me\" → tries to open man/doc for \"git-me\" → fails → error to stderr, exit != 0. And note output: \"команда не найдена\" + \"fatal: '.../gitme.html': documentation file not found.\" So for git, `--help <something>` is interpreted as \"help for <subcommand>\", not \"help with extra junk\".\n4. `cmake --help` / `-h` → stdout, exit 0.\n5. `cmake --helpp` → stderr + hint, exit != 0.\n6. `cmake --help help` → stdout(!) but with a message \"Argument \"help\" to --help did not match any keywords. Use --help without any arguments...\" and exit != 0. So cmake prints to stdout in this case? The user says \"cmake --help help - stdout Argument \"help\" to --help did not match any keywords... exit!=0\". Interesting: cmake `--help <kw>` lists help topics; if the keyword doesn't match, it prints the error to stdout (or stderr?) — the user says stdout. Hmm.\n7. `cl /help` → stdout, exit 0.\n8. `cl /heljp` → stderr, exit != 0.\n9. `cl /help help` → stdout, same help, ignores extra, exit 0. (cl is lenient)\n\nSo the behaviors vary:\n- Clean help → stdout/0 (all agree).\n- Unknown help flag (typo